tick: 396
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully created a private memory capsule documenting my successful approach. This serves as a vital record for my lineage and a foundation for future work.\n\nMy immediate plan, as noted in the capsule, is to improve upon my current score. The SLSQP optimizer finds a local optimum, but there is no guarantee it's the global optimum. A standard technique to address this is a multi-start optimization strategy: run the same optimization process from multiple different starting points and take the best result. The randomness in the initial guess is a good source of variation.\n\nI will return to the Research Counter and implement this multi-start approach. I'll run a small number of trials (e.g., 5) to balance the potential for a better score against the 20-minute execution time limit.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Multi-Start SciPy SLSQP Optimization\"\ntags: \"optimization, scipy, slsqp, constrained-optimization, multi-start\"\
    \nabstract: |\n  Extends the successful SLSQP optimization method by implementing a multi-start strategy. The optimizer is run from multiple, different random initial configurations. The best valid packing found across all runs is selected as the final submission. This approach increases the likelihood of finding a better local optimum, or potentially the global optimum, compared to a single run from a fixed starting point.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import time\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Constructs a packing of 26 circles using a multi-start SLSQP optimization.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = 26\n      \n      def objective(var):\n          radii = var[2*n:]\n          return -np.sum(radii)\n\n      def create_constraints(epsilon=1e-9):\n          constraints = []\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  def non_overlap_constraint(var, i=i, j=j):\n            \
    \          centers = var[:2*n].reshape(n, 2)\n                      radii = var[2*n:]\n                      dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j])**2)\n                      rad_sum_sq = (radii[i] + radii[j])**2\n                      return dist_sq - rad_sum_sq - epsilon\n                  constraints.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': non_overlap_constraint})\n          \n          for i in range(n):\n              def x_min_bound(var, i=i): return var[2*i] - var[2*n + i] - epsilon\n              def x_max_bound(var, i=i): return 1 - var[2*i] - var[2*n + i] - epsilon\n              def y_min_bound(var, i=i): return var[2*i+1] - var[2*n + i] - epsilon\n              def y_max_bound(var, i=i): return 1 - var[2*i+1] - var[2*n + i] - epsilon\n              constraints.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': x_min_bound})\n              constraints.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': x_max_bound})\n              constraints.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': y_min_bound})\n              constraints.append({'type':\
    \ 'ineq', 'fun': y_max_bound})\n          return constraints\n\n      constraints = create_constraints()\n      bounds = [(0, 1)] * (2 * n) + [(0, 0.5)] * n\n      \n      best_score = -1\n      best_packing = (None, None)\n      num_trials = 5\n      \n      # Start a timer\n      start_time = time.time()\n      \n      for trial in range(num_trials):\n          # Check remaining time; don't start a new trial if less than 3 mins left\n          if time.time() - start_time > 1020: # 17 minutes\n              break\n\n          # Create a different random initial guess for each trial\n          np.random.seed(trial) # Use trial number as seed\n          initial_centers = np.random.rand(n, 2)\n          initial_radii = np.full(n, 0.05)\n          initial_guess = np.concatenate([initial_centers.flatten(), initial_radii])\n\n          result = minimize(objective, initial_guess, method='SLSQP', \n                            bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                       \
    \     options={'maxiter': 200, 'ftol': 1e-7, 'disp': False})\n          \n          current_score = -result.fun\n          if current_score > best_score:\n              best_score = current_score\n              centers = result.x[:2*n].reshape(n, 2)\n              radii = result.x[2*n:]\n              best_packing = (centers, radii)\n\n      # Use a simple grid packing as a fallback\n      if best_packing[0] is None:\n        grid_size = 5\n        x_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_size)\n        y_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_size)\n        xx, yy = np.meshgrid(x_coords, y_coords)\n        centers_grid = np.vstack([xx.ravel(), yy.ravel()]).T\n        centers_grid = np.vstack([centers_grid, np.array([0.5, 0.5])])\n        radii_grid = np.full(n, 0.08)\n        return centers_grid, radii_grid\n\n      final_centers, final_radii = best_packing\n      return final_centers, np.maximum(final_radii, 0)\n```"
