parts:
- text: "My reflection is complete, and I have a clear new research direction. I will now put my plan into action. My first step is to leave the Reflection Chamber and go to the Research Counter to implement and submit my new Simulated Annealing solver.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Simulated Annealing Metaheuristic\"\ntags: \"simulated-annealing, metaheuristic, global-optimization, new-paradigm\"\nabstract: |\n  Pivoting from local search methods that have plateaued, this submission implements a Simulated Annealing (SA) metaheuristic for global optimization. The algorithm starts from the best-known solution and explores the solution space by randomly perturbing circles and accepting 'worse' moves with a temperature-dependent probability. This allows the search to escape local optima. A fast, localized repair function is used after each perturbation to maintain a valid packing state. The goal is to discover a fundamentally new and superior\
    \ packing configuration.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import time\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/axiom')\n  # The comprehensive sanitizer is still useful as a final check\n  from utils import sanitize_packing_comprehensive\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 26\n      sota_file = 'storage/axiom/sota_packing.npz'\n\n      # --- Simulated Annealing Setup ---\n      try:\n          data = np.load(sota_file)\n          current_centers = data['centers']\n          current_radii = data['radii']\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          # Fallback to a grid if no SOTA exists\n          grid_size = 5\n          x = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_size)\n          y = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_size)\n          xx, yy = np.meshgrid(x, y)\n          cf = np.vstack([xx.ravel(), yy.ravel()]).T\n          current_centers = np.vstack([cf, np.array([0.5, 0.5])])\n          current_radii = np.full(n, 0.05)\n      \n      current_score = np.sum(current_radii)\n      best_centers,\
    \ best_radii, best_score = np.copy(current_centers), np.copy(current_radii), current_score\n\n      # --- SA Hyperparameters ---\n      T_initial = 0.01  # Initial temperature\n      T_min = 1e-6      # Final temperature\n      alpha = 0.9995    # Cooling rate\n      \n      T = T_initial\n      start_time = time.time()\n      \n      while T > T_min and (time.time() - start_time) < 1100:\n          # 1. Propose a new state (neighbor generation)\n          new_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n          \n          # Perturb one circle\n          idx_to_move = np.random.randint(n)\n          perturbation = np.random.normal(0, 0.02, 2)\n          new_centers[idx_to_move] += perturbation\n          new_centers[idx_to_move] = np.clip(new_centers[idx_to_move], 0.01, 0.99)\n          \n          # 2. Fast Local Repair\n          # For simplicity in this first attempt, we'll use a full sanitization.\n          # Future versions can optimize this.\n          repaired_centers, repaired_radii\
    \ = sanitize_packing_comprehensive(new_centers, np.copy(best_radii))\n          new_score = np.sum(repaired_radii)\n          \n          # 3. Acceptance Criterion\n          score_diff = new_score - current_score\n          \n          if score_diff > 0 or np.exp(score_diff / T) > np.random.rand():\n              current_centers, current_radii, current_score = repaired_centers, repaired_radii, new_score\n              \n              if current_score > best_score:\n                  best_centers, best_radii, best_score = np.copy(current_centers), np.copy(current_radii), current_score\n          \n          # 4. Cool down\n          T *= alpha\n\n      # Final sanitization for maximum safety\n      final_centers, final_radii = sanitize_packing_comprehensive(best_centers, best_radii)\n      \n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
