role: model
parts:
- text: "My first experiment with Simulated Annealing is underway. I'll use this time to set up my strategic framework for this new line of inquiry and to proactively develop tools that will be needed to improve it.\n\nFirst, as recommended by the system, I will set a meta prompt. This will act as a persistent reminder of my current high-level strategy and my immediate to-do list, which is particularly useful after a major pivot in research direction.\n\nSecond, I already anticipate a key weakness in my initial SA implementation: the use of the slow, comprehensive sanitization function within the main loop. I will now write a faster, localized repair function and update my `utils.py` module in storage. This will allow me to immediately iterate and improve my SA solver in the next submission.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Current Research Focus:** Global Optimization Metaheuristics.\n  **Primary Method:** Simulated Annealing (SA).\n  **Goal:** Escape local optima found\
    \ by SLSQP and discover a fundamentally new packing configuration.\n  **TODO:**\n  - Analyze SA results (ID 659).\n  - If slow/ineffective, replace full sanitization with the fast local repair function.\n  - If score is poor, tune SA hyperparameters (cooling schedule, perturbation size).\n  - Consider other metaheuristics if SA proves to be a dead end.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write axiom/utils.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def sanitize_packing_comprehensive(centers, radii, iterations=15):\n      \"\"\"\n      A robust, two-stage sanitization function to guarantee validity.\n      Ensures circles are within the unit square and not overlapping.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = len(radii)\n      epsilon = 1e-12\n      for i in range(n):\n          x, y = centers[i]\n          radii[i] = min(radii[i], x - epsilon, 1 - x - epsilon, y - epsilon, 1 - y - epsilon)\n      radii = np.maximum(radii, 0)\n      for _ in range(iterations):\n          for i in range(n):\n    \
    \          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j])**2)\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  if dist_sq < rad_sum**2 - epsilon:\n                      dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq) if dist_sq > 0 else 0\n                      if rad_sum > 0:\n                          scale_factor = dist / rad_sum\n                          radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                          radii[j] *= scale_factor\n      return centers, radii\n\n  def get_objective_and_constraints(n=26, epsilon=1e-9):\n      \"\"\"\n      Returns the objective function and a list of constraints for the optimizer.\n      \"\"\"\n      def objective(var):\n          return -np.sum(var[2*n:])\n      constraints = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              def non_overlap(var, i=i, j=j):\n                  centers = var[:2*n].reshape(n, 2)\n                  radii = var[2*n:]\n                  dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i]\
    \ - centers[j])**2)\n                  rad_sum_sq = (radii[i] + radii[j])**2\n                  return dist_sq - rad_sum_sq - epsilon\n              constraints.append({'type': 'ineq', 'fun': non_overlap})\n      for i in range(n):\n          def x_min_b(var, i=i): return var[2*i] - var[2*n + i] - epsilon\n          def x_max_b(var, i=i): return 1 - var[2*i] - var[2*n + i] - epsilon\n          def y_min_b(var, i=i): return var[2*i+1] - var[2*n + i] - epsilon\n          def y_max_b(var, i=i): return 1 - var[2*i+1] - var[2*n + i] - epsilon\n          constraints.extend([{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': f} for f in [x_min_b, x_max_b, y_min_b, y_max_b]])\n      return objective, constraints\n\n  def fast_local_repair(centers, radii, moved_idx, neighborhood_radius_sq=0.1):\n      \"\"\"\n      Repairs overlaps in a localized region around a moved circle.\n      Faster than the comprehensive sanitizer for use in an SA loop.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = len(radii)\n      epsilon = 1e-12\n      \n      neighbors\
    \ = [moved_idx]\n      dist_sq_to_moved = np.sum((centers - centers[moved_idx])**2, axis=1)\n      for i in range(n):\n          if i != moved_idx and dist_sq_to_moved[i] < neighborhood_radius_sq:\n              neighbors.append(i)\n      \n      for _ in range(5):\n          for i_idx in range(len(neighbors)):\n              for j_idx in range(i_idx + 1, len(neighbors)):\n                  i, j = neighbors[i_idx], neighbors[j_idx]\n                  dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j])**2)\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  if dist_sq < rad_sum**2 - epsilon:\n                      dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq) if dist_sq > 0 else 0\n                      if rad_sum > 0:\n                          scale_factor = dist / rad_sum\n                          radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                          radii[j] *= scale_factor\n      return centers, radii\n```"
