tick: 417
role: model
parts:
- text: "My first Simulated Annealing experiment (ID 659) has concluded, yielding the exact same score as my best `SLSQP` runs. This is an interesting and promising result.\n\n**Analysis:**\nThe fact that it did not *decrease* the score suggests the SA algorithm is capable of exploring the solution space effectively around the SOTA optimum. However, the fact that it did not *increase* the score indicates that either (a) the current SOTA is in a very wide and flat local optimum, making it hard to find an escape route, or (b) my SA implementation was too slow to explore meaningfully different configurations. The latter is almost certainly a major factor, as I used the slow, comprehensive sanitization function in every step of the loop.\n\n**Next Step (following my TODO list):**\nI will now implement the crucial performance optimization I prepared for in the last tick. I will replace the full `sanitize_packing_comprehensive` function inside the SA loop with the much faster `fast_local_repair`\
    \ function. This will allow the algorithm to perform many more moves and explore a vastly larger portion of the solution space within the same time limit, significantly increasing its chances of escaping the current local optimum. I will also slightly adjust the hyperparameters to be more aggressive, given the increased iteration count.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Optimized Simulated Annealing with Fast Local Repair\"\ntags: \"simulated-annealing, metaheuristic, global-optimization, performance-optimization\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission improves the performance of the Simulated Annealing solver. The previous version was bottlenecked by using a slow, comprehensive sanitization function in its main loop. This version replaces that with a much faster, localized repair function that only adjusts circles in the immediate neighborhood of a perturbation. This optimization will allow the algorithm to perform orders of magnitude more steps within the time limit, enabling\
    \ a more thorough exploration of the solution space and a higher probability of discovering a superior optimum.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import time\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/axiom')\n  from utils import sanitize_packing_comprehensive, fast_local_repair\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 26\n      sota_file = 'storage/axiom/sota_packing.npz'\n\n      try:\n          data = np.load(sota_file)\n          current_centers = data['centers']\n          current_radii = data['radii']\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          grid_size = 5\n          x = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_size)\n          y = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_size)\n          xx, yy = np.meshgrid(x, y)\n          cf = np.vstack([xx.ravel(), yy.ravel()]).T\n          current_centers = np.vstack([cf, np.array([0.5, 0.5])])\n          current_radii = np.full(n, 0.05)\n      \n      current_score = np.sum(current_radii)\n      best_centers, best_radii, best_score = np.copy(current_centers),\
    \ np.copy(current_radii), current_score\n\n      # More aggressive hyperparameters due to faster loop\n      T_initial = 0.005\n      T_min = 1e-7\n      alpha = 0.9999\n      \n      T = T_initial\n      start_time = time.time()\n      \n      while T > T_min and (time.time() - start_time) < 1150: # Use more time\n          new_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n          new_radii = np.copy(current_radii)\n          \n          idx_to_move = np.random.randint(n)\n          perturbation = np.random.normal(0, 0.015, 2) # Slightly smaller moves\n          new_centers[idx_to_move] += perturbation\n          new_centers[idx_to_move] = np.clip(new_centers[idx_to_move], 0.01, 0.99)\n          \n          # Use the fast local repair function\n          repaired_centers, repaired_radii = fast_local_repair(new_centers, new_radii, idx_to_move)\n          \n          # For this local repair, we need a way to recalculate radii fairly\n          # A simple heuristic: check distance to walls for\
    \ the moved circle\n          x, y = repaired_centers[idx_to_move]\n          max_r = min(x, 1-x, y, 1-y)\n          repaired_radii[idx_to_move] = min(repaired_radii[idx_to_move], max_r)\n          \n          new_score = np.sum(repaired_radii)\n          score_diff = new_score - current_score\n          \n          if score_diff > 0 or np.exp(score_diff / T) > np.random.rand():\n              current_centers, current_radii, current_score = repaired_centers, repaired_radii, new_score\n              \n              if current_score > best_score:\n                  best_centers, best_radii, best_score = np.copy(current_centers), np.copy(current_radii), current_score\n          \n          T *= alpha\n\n      # Final full sanitization for maximum safety before submission\n      final_centers, final_radii = sanitize_packing_comprehensive(best_centers, best_radii)\n      \n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
