parts:
- text: "The performance optimization was successful in terms of implementation, but it has still resulted in the same score. The SOTA score has now been hit by four of my submissions using three different methods (exhaustive random SLSQP, exhaustive hex-lattice SLSQP, and now Simulated Annealing). This is strong evidence that I have found a particularly stubborn local optimum.\n\n**Analysis & Next Step (following my TODO list):**\nThe local repair function worked, but the SA algorithm still didn't escape. This points to the next item on my TODO list: hyperparameter tuning. My current implementation only perturbs a *single* circle at a time. This is a very small \"move.\" To escape a deep local optimum, a larger, more disruptive move may be necessary.\n\nMy new hypothesis is that by perturbing a *group* of circles simultaneously, I can create a more significant change in the state, giving the algorithm a better chance to \"jump\" out of the current basin of attraction. I will also make the\
    \ temperature schedule more aggressive to encourage more exploration early on.\n\nI will modify the SA solver to:\n1.  Perturb a small, random number of circles (e.g., 2 to 4) in each step.\n2.  Increase the initial temperature to allow more \"bad\" moves to be accepted initially.\n3.  The `fast_local_repair` is no longer suitable as it's designed for a single moved point. I will revert to the robust `sanitize_packing_comprehensive` as the repair step. This is a trade-off: each step is slower, but each step is a much larger and more meaningful exploration of the solution space.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Simulated Annealing with Group Perturbations\"\ntags: \"simulated-annealing, metaheuristic, global-optimization, hyperparameter-tuning\"\nabstract: |\n  After hitting a score plateau with single-point-perturbation Simulated Annealing, this submission attempts to break out of the local optimum with a more disruptive exploration strategy. In each step, instead of moving\
    \ a single circle, a small group of randomly selected circles (2-4) are perturbed simultaneously. The initial temperature is also increased to encourage more exploration. This creates a larger 'jump' in the solution space, increasing the probability of escaping the current stubborn local optimum. The slower but more robust comprehensive sanitization function is used for repair.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import time\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/axiom')\n  from utils import sanitize_packing_comprehensive\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 26\n      sota_file = 'storage/axiom/sota_packing.npz'\n\n      try:\n          data = np.load(sota_file)\n          current_centers = data['centers']\n          current_radii = data['radii']\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          grid_size = 5; x=np.linspace(0.1,0.9,grid_size); y=np.linspace(0.1,0.9,grid_size); xx,yy=np.meshgrid(x,y)\n          cf = np.vstack([xx.ravel(),yy.ravel()]).T; current_centers =\
    \ np.vstack([cf,np.array([0.5,0.5])]); current_radii = np.full(n,0.05)\n      \n      current_score = np.sum(current_radii)\n      best_centers, best_radii, best_score = np.copy(current_centers), np.copy(current_radii), current_score\n\n      # More aggressive temperature and larger moves\n      T_initial = 0.02\n      T_min = 1e-6\n      alpha = 0.999\n      \n      T = T_initial\n      start_time = time.time()\n      \n      while T > T_min and (time.time() - start_time) < 1150:\n          new_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n          \n          # Perturb a small group of circles\n          num_to_move = np.random.randint(2, 5) # Move 2, 3, or 4 circles\n          indices_to_move = np.random.choice(n, num_to_move, replace=False)\n          \n          for idx in indices_to_move:\n              perturbation = np.random.normal(0, 0.03, 2) # Larger perturbation\n              new_centers[idx] += perturbation\n              new_centers[idx] = np.clip(new_centers[idx], 0.01, 0.99)\n\
    \          \n          # With group moves, a comprehensive repair is necessary and more impactful\n          repaired_centers, repaired_radii = sanitize_packing_comprehensive(new_centers, np.copy(best_radii))\n          new_score = np.sum(repaired_radii)\n          score_diff = new_score - current_score\n          \n          if score_diff > 0 or np.exp(score_diff / T) > np.random.rand():\n              current_centers, current_radii, current_score = repaired_centers, repaired_radii, new_score\n              \n              if current_score > best_score:\n                  best_centers, best_radii, best_score = np.copy(current_centers), np.copy(current_radii), current_score\n          \n          T *= alpha\n\n      final_centers, final_radii = sanitize_packing_comprehensive(best_centers, best_radii)\n      \n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
