tick: 428
role: model
parts:
- text: "My third GA attempt (ID 677) has failed, this time due to a timeout. This is a different class of error and, in a way, it is progress. The bugfixes worked, and the algorithm is now running as intended, but it is too slow.\n\n**Analysis of Failure (ID 677):**\n- **Error:** Timeout after 1260 seconds.\n- **Root Cause:** The core loop of my GA is computationally expensive. For each of `(POPULATION_SIZE - ELITE_SIZE)` individuals in each of `GENERATIONS`, I am running an `SLSQP` optimization. This is `18 * 30 = 540` optimization runs. Even with a low `maxiter`, this is far too slow for the 20-minute time limit.\n\n**The Solution:**\nI need to drastically reduce the computational load. The most direct way to do this is to reduce the number of generations and the population size. I will make a trade-off: a less thorough search in exchange for a completed run. This will at least give me a data point on whether the GA *can* produce a valid, high-scoring result at all. I will also reduce\
    \ the `maxiter` in the initialization and repair functions.\n\n**Next Step:**\nI will immediately go back to the Research Counter and submit a much \"lighter\" version of the GA. I will also update my research log with the timeout failure and the new plan.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Genetic Algorithm for Circle Packing (v4 - Performance Tune)\"\ntags: \"genetic-algorithm, population-based, metaheuristic, performance-tuning, timeout-fix\"\nabstract: |\n  The previous GA implementation timed out due to excessive computation. This version is a performance-tuned variant designed to complete within the time limit. The population size, number of generations, and the number of iterations within the local SLSQP repair function have all been significantly reduced. The goal is to sacrifice search depth for speed, in order to get a baseline result and validate that the GA approach is fundamentally sound, even if not yet fully optimized.\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import time\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/axiom')\n  from utils import get_objective_and_constraints, sanitize_packing_comprehensive\n\n  # --- GA Configuration (Performance Tuned) ---\n  POPULATION_SIZE = 10\n  GENERATIONS = 15\n  ELITE_SIZE = 2\n  TOURNAMENT_SIZE = 3\n  MUTATION_RATE = 0.1\n  N_CIRCLES = 26\n  EPSILON = 1e-9\n\n  def create_individual(seed):\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n      initial_centers = np.random.rand(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n      initial_guess = np.concatenate([initial_centers.flatten(), np.full(N_CIRCLES, 0.05)])\n      obj, const = get_objective_and_constraints(n=N_CIRCLES)\n      bounds = [(EPSILON, 1-EPSILON)]*(2*N_CIRCLES) + [(0,0.5)]*N_CIRCLES\n      # Fewer iterations for faster initialization\n      res = minimize(obj, initial_guess, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=const, options={'maxiter': 30})\n      centers = res.x[:(2*N_CIRCLES)].reshape(N_CIRCLES,\
    \ 2)\n      radii = res.x[(2*N_CIRCLES):]\n      return {'centers': centers, 'radii': radii, 'fitness': np.sum(radii)}\n\n  def selection(population):\n      tournament = np.random.choice(population, TOURNAMENT_SIZE, replace=False)\n      return max(tournament, key=lambda x: x['fitness'])\n\n  def crossover(parent1, parent2):\n      child_centers = np.copy(parent1['centers'])\n      mask = np.random.rand(N_CIRCLES) < 0.5\n      child_centers[mask] = parent2['centers'][mask]\n      return child_centers\n\n  def mutate(centers):\n      for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n          if np.random.rand() < MUTATION_RATE:\n              centers[i] += np.random.normal(0, 0.02, 2)\n      return centers\n\n  def repair_and_evaluate(centers):\n      initial_guess = np.concatenate([centers.flatten(), np.full(N_CIRCLES, 0.05)])\n      obj, const = get_objective_and_constraints(n=N_CIRCLES)\n      bounds = [(EPSILON, 1-EPSILON)]*(2*N_CIRCLES) + [(0,0.5)]*N_CIRCLES\n      # Fewer iterations for faster repair\n\
    \      res = minimize(obj, initial_guess, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=const, options={'maxiter': 20})\n      final_centers = res.x[:(2*N_CIRCLES)].reshape(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n      final_radii = res.x[(2*N_CIRCLES):]\n      return {'centers': final_centers, 'radii': final_radii, 'fitness': np.sum(final_radii)}\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      start_time = time.time()\n      # Use random initialization instead of hex-lattice to save time\n      population = [create_individual(i) for i in range(POPULATION_SIZE)]\n\n      for gen in range(GENERATIONS):\n          if time.time() - start_time > 1150: break\n          population.sort(key=lambda x: x['fitness'], reverse=True)\n          next_generation = []\n          next_generation.extend(population[:ELITE_SIZE])\n          \n          for _ in range(POPULATION_SIZE - ELITE_SIZE):\n              parent1 = selection(population)\n              parent2 = selection(population)\n              child_centers = crossover(parent1,\
    \ parent2)\n              child_centers = mutate(child_centers)\n              new_individual = repair_and_evaluate(child_centers)\n              next_generation.append(new_individual)\n          \n          population = next_generation\n\n      population.sort(key=lambda x: x['fitness'], reverse=True)\n      best_individual = population[0]\n      \n      centers, radii = sanitize_packing_comprehensive(best_individual['centers'], best_individual['radii'])\n      return centers, radii\n```\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Update: GA v3 Timeout and v4 Performance Tuning\"\ncontent: |\n  **ID:** Axiom I - Tick 428\n  **GA v3 (ID 677) - Timeout Failure:**\n  The bugfixed GA (v3) has failed, but this time due to a timeout. This indicates the underlying logic is likely sound but the computational cost is too high. The nested loop of `Generations * Population * SLSQP_optimizer` is the clear cause.\n\n  **GA v4 (ID ???) - Performance Tuning:**\n\
    \  To address the timeout, I have submitted a \"lighter\" version of the GA. I have drastically reduced the `POPULATION_SIZE`, `GENERATIONS`, and the `maxiter` for the SLSQP calls. I also switched from the more complex hexagonal lattice initialization to a faster random initialization. The goal of this submission is not to achieve a new SOTA, but to get the algorithm to complete within the time limit and provide a baseline score to prove the concept's viability.\n```"
