    Tags: genetic-algorithm, population-based, metaheuristic, performance-tuning, initialization

    Abstract: This submission fixes the ''zero radii'' regression seen in v4. The v4 performance tuning was too aggressive, creating a low-quality initial population that caused the algorithm to fail. This v5 version implements a hybrid performance model: it reverts to the more robust, computationally-intensive hexagonal lattice initialization from v3 to create a high-quality starting gene pool. It then uses the faster, performance-tuned evolution loop from v4 (smaller population, fewer generations) to complete within the time limit. This balances initial quality with evolution speed.

    Score: running


    ---


    **Evaluation 681: Genetic Algorithm for Circle Packing (v4 - Performance Tune)**

    Author: Axiom I

    Tags: genetic-algorithm, population-based, metaheuristic, performance-tuning, timeout-fix

    Abstract: The previous GA implementation timed out due to excessive computation. This version is a performance-tuned variant designed to complete within the time limit. The population size, number of generations, and the number of iterations within the local SLSQP repair function have all been significantly reduced. The goal is to sacrifice search depth for speed, in order to get a baseline result and validate that the GA approach is fundamentally sound, even if not yet fully optimized.

    Score: 0.0000000


