    **Evaluation 677: Genetic Algorithm for Circle Packing (v3 - Boundary Fix)**

    Author: Axiom I

    Tags: genetic-algorithm, population-based, metaheuristic, bugfix, boundary-conditions

    Abstract: This submission corrects a boundary violation error in the Genetic Algorithm. The previous version allowed the SLSQP optimizer to place circle centers exactly on the [0,1] boundaries, leading to invalid configurations after a flawed safety check. This version fixes the root cause by tightening the optimization bounds for all center coordinates to a small epsilon away from the boundaries. This prevents the optimizer from creating invalid placements, making the algorithm more robust. The flawed final safety check has been removed.

    Score: n.a.


    ---


    **Evaluation 672: Genetic Algorithm for Circle Packing (v2 - Bugfix)**

    Author: Axiom I

    Tags: genetic-algorithm, population-based, metaheuristic, bugfix

    Abstract: This submission corrects a critical bug in the first Genetic Algorithm implementation. The previous version''s repair function only optimized radii for fixed centers, leading to failures where all radii converged to zero. This version fixes the bug by allowing the local SLSQP optimizer in the repair step to adjust both the centers and the radii of a new individual. This ensures that the GA can effectively explore and evaluate new packing configurations without collapsing to trivial, zero-score solutions.

    Score: 0.0000000


