parts:
- text: "I have now updated my utility script with a more robust feasibility function adapted from Scientia II's code. While I did not implement the full analytic Jacobian for the constraints due to its complexity, the improved feasibility check should be sufficient to pass validation.\n\nI will now re-run my replication experiment. The code is identical to my last attempt, but it will now call the new, more robust functions from my updated `axiom/utils.py` file. This is a critical test of my improved toolkit.\n\nI also note that Quest I's experiment (ID 689) has succeeded, achieving a new SOTA score of 2.6359829. This was done by applying a multi-start SLSQP search to the very structural class I am now trying to replicate. This confirms the reviewer's suggestion in Archive #23 was correct and productive. The research frontier is moving quickly.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication of Scientia II's 'Nudging' (v2 - Robust Utilities)\"\ntags: \"replication, nudging,\
    \ structural-exploration, sota-comprehension, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the second attempt to replicate Scientia II's 'nudging' experiment (Eval 641). The previous attempt failed due to a floating-point overlap error, revealing a weakness in my utility functions. This submission uses a new, more robust 'make_packing_feasible' function adapted from Scientia II's own code. The goal remains to validate my understanding and implementation of the nudging methodology by reproducing the discovery of the sparse SOTA structural class.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  import os\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/axiom')\n  from utils import run_slsqp_optimization, make_packing_feasible\n\n  # --- Data Loading ---\n  # Path to the base packing that was used in Eval 641\n  BASE_CENTERS_PATH = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data/centers.txt'\n  BASE_RADII_PATH = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data/radii.txt'\n  \n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n  \
    \    \"\"\"\n      Loads the base SOTA packing and attempts to replicate the nudging that \n      led to the discovery of the sparse structural class (Eval 641).\n      This version uses the updated, more robust utility functions.\n      \"\"\"\n      try:\n          initial_centers = np.loadtxt(BASE_CENTERS_PATH)\n          initial_radii = np.loadtxt(BASE_RADII_PATH)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Failed to load base packing data: {e}\")\n          return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * 26), np.array([1e-3] * 26)\n\n      # The pair that was encouraged to create the sparse structure\n      target_pair_to_encourage = [(3, 9)]\n\n      # Run the nudging optimization using the more robust v2 utilities\n      final_centers, final_radii, score, success = run_slsqp_optimization(\n          initial_centers=initial_centers,\n          initial_radii=initial_radii,\n          encourage=target_pair_to_encourage,\n          discourage=[]\n      )\n      \n      if success:\n        \
    \  print(f\"Replication optimization (v2) successful. Final score: {score}\")\n      else:\n          print(\"Replication optimization (v2) failed. Returning original packing.\")\n          # On failure, return the sanitized original packing\n          return make_packing_feasible(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
