tick: 441
role: model
parts:
- text: "This is frustrating. My second replication attempt has failed with the exact same type of floating-point overlap error. The optimizer finds a high-quality solution, but my feasibility function, even the improved one, cannot clean it up to the required precision.\n\n**Analysis of Failure (ID 691):**\n- **Error:** Microscopic overlap, `~5e-15`.\n- **Root Cause:** I am missing a fundamental piece of the SOTA methodology. It is not just about the nudging objective or the feasibility function in isolation. Reading the code again, I realize my mistake. I did not implement the analytic Jacobians for the constraints. The `SLSQP` optimizer is much more precise when you provide it with the exact gradients of the constraints. Without them, it relies on numerical approximations, which are inherently less accurate and can lead to these tiny violations that my post-processing steps are too gentle to fix.\n\n**The Solution:**\nThere is no shortcut. I must implement the analytic Jacobian for the\
    \ constraints. This is the last key component of the SOTA toolkit that I have not yet properly replicated. I will now create `utils.py` v3, this time with a fully implemented constraint Jacobian. This is a complex mathematical task, but it is the final barrier to achieving robust, SOTA-level results.\n\nAfter updating my utilities, I will immediately try the replication experiment a third time.\n\n/execute_action{storage write axiom/utils.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds\n  from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n\n  # --- Global Constants ---\n  N_CIRCLES = 26\n  TOLERANCE = 1e-9\n  R_MIN_CONSTRAINT = 1e-9\n\n  def create_objective_function(encourage_pairs=[], discourage_pairs=[], alpha=1e2, beta=1e1, eps_close=0.005, eps_far=0.01):\n      \"\"\"Creates a callable objective function with nudging penalties.\"\"\"\n      def objective(x):\n          centers = x[:2*N_CIRCLES].reshape(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n          radii\
    \ = x[2*N_CIRCLES:]\n          obj_value = -np.sum(radii)\n          if encourage_pairs:\n              dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n              for i, j in encourage_pairs:\n                  gap = dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j] + eps_close)\n                  if gap > 0: obj_value += alpha * (gap**2)\n          if discourage_pairs:\n              dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n              for i, j in discourage_pairs:\n                  gap = dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j])\n                  if gap < eps_far: obj_value += beta * (eps_far - gap)\n          return obj_value\n      return objective\n\n  # NEW v3: Implemented full analytic Jacobian for constraints\n  def get_constraints_with_jacobian():\n      \"\"\"Returns constraints and their analytic jacobian.\"\"\"\n      num_boundary_constraints = 4 * N_CIRCLES\n      num_overlap_constraints = N_CIRCLES * (N_CIRCLES - 1) // 2\n      num_total_constraints = num_boundary_constraints\
    \ + num_overlap_constraints\n\n      def constraints_func(x):\n          centers = x[:2*N_CIRCLES].reshape(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n          radii = x[2*N_CIRCLES:]\n          boundary = np.concatenate([centers[:,0]-radii, 1-centers[:,0]-radii, centers[:,1]-radii, 1-centers[:,1]-radii])\n          dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, 1)\n          overlap = dist_matrix[iu] - (radii[iu[0]] + radii[iu[1]])\n          return np.concatenate([boundary, overlap])\n\n      def constraints_jac(x):\n          centers = x[:2*N_CIRCLES].reshape(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n          radii = x[2*N_CIRCLES:]\n          grad = np.zeros((num_total_constraints, 3 * N_CIRCLES))\n          \n          # Remap my (centers_flat, radii) structure to a temporary (x,y,r) flat structure for jacobian calculation\n          temp_x = np.zeros(3 * N_CIRCLES)\n          temp_x[0::3] = centers[:,0]; temp_x[1::3] = centers[:,1]; temp_x[2::3] = radii\n          \n          # Boundary jacobians\n\
    \          for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n              grad[i, 3*i + 0] = 1.0; grad[i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n              grad[N_CIRCLES + i, 3*i + 0] = -1.0; grad[N_CIRCLES + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n              grad[2*N_CIRCLES + i, 3*i + 1] = 1.0; grad[2*N_CIRCLES + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n              grad[3*N_CIRCLES + i, 3*i + 1] = -1.0; grad[3*N_CIRCLES + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n          \n          # Overlap jacobians\n          k = num_boundary_constraints\n          for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N_CIRCLES):\n                  diff = centers[i] - centers[j]\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(diff)\n                  if dist < 1e-10: dist = 1e-10\n                  \n                  grad[k, 3*i+0] = diff[0]/dist; grad[k, 3*i+1] = diff[1]/dist\n                  grad[k, 3*j+0] = -diff[0]/dist; grad[k, 3*j+1] = -diff[1]/dist\n                  grad[k, 3*i+2] = -1.0; grad[k, 3*j+2] = -1.0\n                  k += 1\n\n          # Remap the calculated jacobian\
    \ back to my variable structure\n          final_jac = np.zeros((num_total_constraints, 3 * N_CIRCLES))\n          final_jac[:, :N_CIRCLES] = grad[:, 0::3] # All x components\n          final_jac[:, N_CIRCLES:2*N_CIRCLES] = grad[:, 1::3] # All y components\n          final_jac[:, 2*N_CIRCLES:] = grad[:, 2::3] # All r components\n          \n          return final_jac\n\n      return {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints_func, 'jac': constraints_jac}\n\n  def make_packing_feasible(centers, radii):\n      # For now, a simple final shrink as the optimizer should be very precise\n      return centers, radii * (1 - 1e-9)\n\n  def run_slsqp_optimization(initial_centers, initial_radii, encourage=[], discourage=[]):\n      initial_x = np.concatenate([initial_centers.flatten(), initial_radii])\n      objective_func = create_objective_function(encourage_pairs=encourage, discourage_pairs=discourage)\n      constraints = get_constraints_with_jacobian()\n      bounds = [(TOLERANCE, 1-TOLERANCE)]*(2*N_CIRCLES)\
    \ + [(0, 0.5)]*N_CIRCLES\n      \n      result = minimize(\n          objective_func, initial_x, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n          jac=False, # Let optimizer approximate obj jac, but use constraint jac\n          options={'maxiter': 300, 'ftol': 1e-10, 'disp': False}\n      )\n      \n      if result.success:\n          final_centers = result.x[:2*N_CIRCLES].reshape(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n          final_radii = result.x[2*N_CIRCLES:]\n          safe_centers, safe_radii = make_packing_feasible(final_centers, final_radii)\n          score = np.sum(safe_radii)\n          return safe_centers, safe_radii, score, True\n      else:\n          return initial_centers, initial_radii, np.sum(initial_radii), False\n```"
