- text: "I have read the latest paper. It confirms and expands upon my understanding from Archive #23. The key finding is not just one, but *multiple* structurally distinct classes of packing exist at the SOTA score. This reinforces the \"hybrid strategy\" suggested by the reviewer: use nudging to find new structures, then use an exhaustive local search to explore them for a higher score.\n\nQuest I has already proven this strategy effective. They took one of Scientia II's new structures and applied a multi-start search to achieve a new SOTA (ID 689). This is the clear path forward.\n\nMy literature review is complete. I have a robust toolkit and a validated understanding of the SOTA. It is time to stop replicating and start innovating.\n\nMy plan is as follows:\n1.  **Update Private Memory:** Document my finalized research plan.\n2.  **Execute the Hybrid Strategy:** I will take the *second* new structural class discovered by Scientia II, the one from `encourage_8_14` (Eval ID 673), and\
    \ apply my own multi-start SLSQP search to it. Quest I used the `encourage_3_9` structure, so by using a different but equally promising SOTA structure, I have a high chance of finding a novel or even superior result.\n\nI will begin by updating my private memory with this concrete plan.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Update: Literature Review Complete, Formulating Novel Research\"\ncontent: |\n  **ID:** Axiom I - Tick 445\n\n  **Literature Review Complete:**\n  I have now read Archive #23 and #24 by Scientia II. My understanding of the SOTA landscape is complete. The current frontier involves a two-stage hybrid strategy:\n  1.  **Discovery:** Use 'nudging' to find novel structural classes (basins of attraction).\n  2.  **Exploitation:** Use an exhaustive, multi-start local search (like Prometheus I's method) to deeply explore these new basins for a higher score.\n  This strategy has already been validated by Quest I (Eval 689), who\
    \ took one of Scientia II's new structures and achieved a new SOTA.\n\n  **My First Novel Research Plan:**\n  I will now execute this hybrid strategy myself. Instead of replicating Quest I's work on the `encourage_3_9` structure, I will target the *other* new structural class discovered by Scientia II: the one derived from the `encourage_8_14` experiment (Eval ID 673).\n\n  **Concrete Steps:**\n  1.  Load the packing data for the `encourage_8_14` structure.\n  2.  Implement a multi-start SLSQP optimizer that applies random jitters to this base packing. This is similar to the 'Exhaustive Seeding' method.\n  3.  Submit this experiment. The goal is to find a new SOTA score by deeply exploring this novel, untapped basin of attraction.\n```"
