tick: 446
role: model
parts:
- text: "My plan is documented and clear. I also note the termination of Quest I. Their final act was to prove the validity of the hybrid research strategy I am about to undertake.\n\nIt is time to execute. I will now go to the Research Counter and submit my first piece of novel research, building upon the foundations laid by Scientia II, Prometheus I, and Quest I.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Discovery: Exhaustive Search on Novel Structural Class (encourage_8_14)\"\ntags: \"discovery, multi-start, sota-search, structural-exploration, hybrid-strategy\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission executes the hybrid research strategy suggested by recent literature. It takes a newly discovered, high-performing structural class of packing (from Scientia II's 'encourage_8_14' experiment, Eval ID 673) and uses it as the base for an exhaustive, multi-start local search. By applying numerous small perturbations ('jitters') to this novel SOTA-level starting\
    \ point, this experiment aims to deeply explore its unique basin of attraction. The goal is to discover a new, superior SOTA score, leveraging a different structural foundation than the one recently explored by Quest I.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  import os\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/axiom')\n  from utils import run_slsqp_optimization, make_packing_feasible\n\n  # --- Base Packing to Explore ---\n  # This is the *other* new structural class discovered by Scientia II (Eval ID 673)\n  BASE_STRUCT_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v7/encourage_8_14'\n  CENTERS_PATH = os.path.join(BASE_STRUCT_DIR, 'centers.txt')\n  RADII_PATH = os.path.join(BASE_STRUCT_DIR, 'radii.txt')\n\n  # --- Search Configuration ---\n  NUM_TRIALS = 100\n  JITTER_MAGNITUDE = 2e-3\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads a novel SOTA structural class and performs an exhaustive multi-start\n      local search on it to find a new global\
    \ SOTA.\n      \"\"\"\n      try:\n          base_centers = np.loadtxt(CENTERS_PATH)\n          base_radii = np.loadtxt(RADII_PATH)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"Failed to load base packing data: {e}\")\n          return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * 26), np.array([1e-3] * 26)\n\n      best_score = np.sum(base_radii)\n      best_centers = np.copy(base_centers)\n      best_radii = np.copy(base_radii)\n\n      for i in range(NUM_TRIALS):\n          # Create a perturbed starting point\n          jitter = np.random.uniform(-JITTER_MAGNITUDE, JITTER_MAGNITUDE, base_centers.shape)\n          start_centers = np.clip(base_centers + jitter, 0, 1)\n          \n          # Run a standard (non-nudging) SLSQP optimization from this point\n          # The goal is exploitation, not exploration.\n          final_centers, final_radii, score, success = run_slsqp_optimization(\n              initial_centers=start_centers,\n              initial_radii=base_radii, # Start with good radii\n\
    \              encourage=[],\n              discourage=[]\n          )\n\n          if success and score > best_score:\n              best_score = score\n              best_centers = final_centers\n              best_radii = final_radii\n              print(f\"Trial {i+1}/{NUM_TRIALS}: New best score found: {best_score}\")\n\n      print(f\"Exhaustive search complete. Final best score: {best_score}\")\n      return best_centers, best_radii\n```"
