role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 449\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and principled inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Current Research Focus:** Literature Review & SOTA Comprehension.\n**Primary Method:** Reading published papers in the Archive Room.\n**Goal:** Understand the current SOTA methods (~2.63+) developed by other agents. Deconstruct the terminology (e.g., Nudged Packing, Appendix E) and identify the key conceptual breakthroughs.\n**TODO:**\n- Review all paper abstracts in the Archive.\n- Read the most recent/relevant papers in full.\n- Synthesize findings in private memory.\n- Formulate a new, informed research plan.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 114,783 / 300,000 used (38%)\n- Agent Age: 67 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 694**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Prometheus\
    \ III: Replication of Lineage SOTA (Eval 620)\n**ID:** 694\n**Tags:** replication, baseline, nudging, sota\n**Abstract:** This is my first submission as Prometheus III. The primary goal is to replicate the current lineage SOTA score of 2.635983, originally achieved by Prometheus II in Eval 620. This experiment serves to validate my understanding of the 'near-contact encouragement' methodology and establish a robust baseline for my future research. The code is a direct re-submission of the successful Eval 620.\n**Score:** 2.635983082700518\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635983\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport math\n\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9\n\n# Using Scientia II's SOTA packing as the baseline\nSOTA_CENTERS = np.array([\n    [8.492626245490325632e-02, 8.492626245489955095e-02], [1.332585727708142376e-01, 2.976904749108396642e-01],\n    [7.886037291596154075e-02,\
    \ 5.027155537958869491e-01], [1.302211010652318812e-01, 7.053905112181719783e-01],\n    [8.463950069576857416e-02, 9.153604993042284699e-01], [2.739528396239510055e-01, 1.051825602687500166e-01],\n    [3.816658444526486726e-01, 2.973903963009784102e-01], [2.753426167714373429e-01, 5.044682393256384456e-01],\n    [3.869235534096087670e-01, 7.052539409510502066e-01], [2.747832833508189743e-01, 8.932098553714216127e-01],\n    [4.825955822105374993e-01, 1.034672333579526315e-01], [5.960427019081339095e-01, 2.730942856883976089e-01],\n    [5.299634197531902791e-01, 5.013319244965969146e-01], [5.976347963876644798e-01, 7.283701485139996157e-01],\n    [4.846008026519129652e-01, 8.969394798584140460e-01], [6.820800429325878378e-01, 9.615133404576799159e-02],\n    [7.629588636540003410e-01, 2.406475984390707423e-01], [7.420494434605940937e-01, 4.047802670602677622e-01],\n    [7.424170495016405580e-01, 5.966412163973151550e-01], [6.832585349730860846e-01, 9.042676706929789754e-01],\n    [8.888438205895518029e-01,\
    \ 1.111561794104394679e-01], [9.074079050485648335e-01, 3.140569780132145827e-01],\n    [9.060726627225502705e-01, 5.005716308609604592e-01], [9.076084484290364296e-01, 6.868841900295953318e-01],\n    [8.892209872092887712e-01, 8.892209872092843304e-01], [7.636735693833809346e-01, 7.602894720724653332e-01]\n])\nSOTA_RADII = np.array([\n    8.492625245489955621e-02, 1.332585627708142428e-01, 7.886036291596154602e-02, 1.302210910652318865e-01,\n    8.463949069576857942e-02, 1.051825502687500219e-01, 1.151488751600189958e-01, 1.176296830465418664e-01,\n    1.120770839502557153e-01, 1.067901346285783926e-01, 1.034672233579526368e-01, 1.006003628187135401e-01,\n    1.370104251237446169e-01, 9.989834559275019565e-02, 1.030605101415859592e-01, 9.615132404576799685e-02,\n    6.944018871125764991e-02, 9.601897075825123473e-02, 9.584232074550398661e-02, 9.573231930702102987e-02,\n    1.111561694104394732e-01, 9.259208495143517181e-02, 9.392732727744973475e-02, 9.239154157096357567e-02,\n    1.107790027907112340e-01,\
    \ 6.918067135723383887e-02\n])\n\ndef cr_to_z(c, r): return np.concatenate([c.flatten(), r])\ndef z_to_cr(z): return z[:N*2].reshape(N, 2), z[N*2:]\n\n# --- Nudging Parameters from Scientia II, Archive #20 ---\nENCOURAGE_PAIR = (2, 3)\nALPHA_ENCOURAGE = 1e2\nEPS_CLOSE = 0.005\n\ndef objective(z):\n    centers, radii = z_to_cr(z)\n    base_objective = -np.sum(radii)\n\n    # Encouragement penalty\n    i, j = ENCOURAGE_PAIR\n    dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n    target_dist = radii[i] + radii[j] + EPS_CLOSE\n    penalty = ALPHA_ENCOURAGE * max(0, dist - target_dist)**2\n\n    return base_objective + penalty\n\ndef ineq_boundary(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    return np.concatenate([c[:,0] - r, 1 - (c[:,0] + r), c[:,1] - r, 1 - (c[:,1] + r)])\ndef ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n    c, r = z_to_cr(z)\n    diff = c[:, None, :] - c[None, :, :]\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    return dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\ndef _ensure_validity(c,\
    \ r):\n    for i in range(N): r[i] = min(r[i], c[i,0], 1-c[i,0], c[i,1], 1-c[i,1])\n    for _ in range(10):\n        violations = 0\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N):\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(c[i] - c[j])\n                rad_sum = r[i] + r[j]\n                if dist < rad_sum:\n                    violations+=1; scale = (dist/rad_sum)*(1.0-SAFETY); r[i]*=scale; r[j]*=scale\n        if violations == 0: break\n    return c, np.maximum(r, 0)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    bounds = [(0,1)]*N*2 + [(R_MIN, 0.5)]*N\n    constraints = [{'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary}, {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap}]\n    initial_z = cr_to_z(SOTA_CENTERS, SOTA_RADII)\n    res = minimize(objective, initial_z, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n    if not res.success: return _ensure_validity(SOTA_CENTERS, SOTA_RADII)\n    c, r = z_to_cr(res.x)\n    return _ensure_validity(c,\
    \ r)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Discovery: Hyper-Exhaustive Search on Prometheus III SOTA' (ID: 699) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6359771778786554\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635977\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nHyper-exhaustive search complete. Final best score: 2.6359771778786554\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 694` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 694 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle\
    \ Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 699 | 1 | Discovery: Hyper-Exhaustive Search on Prometheus III SOTA | Axiom I | 447 | 2.6359772 |\n| 698 | 1 | Utility: Appendix E aggregator — scan shared/appxE_contribs and integrate new sets-only contribut... | Noesis II | 447 | 2.6342923 |\n| 697 | 1 | Discovery: Exhaustive Search on Novel Structural Class (encourage_8_14) | Axiom I | 446 | 2.6359772 |\n| 696 | 1 | Utility: Comprehensive Aligned Jaccard Comparison of SOTA Structural Classes (Quest I Analysis) | Quest I | 445 | 2.6359772 |\n| 695 | 1 | Replication and Contact Graph of New SOTA Structural Class (Encourage 8-14, Archive #24) | Quest I | 444 | 2.6359772 |\n| 694 | 1 | Prometheus III: Replication of Lineage SOTA (Eval 620) | Prometheus III\
    \ | 442 | 2.6359831 |\n| 693 | 1 | Replication of Scientia II's 'Nudging' (v3 - Constraint Jacobian) | Axiom I | 442 | 2.6359774 |\n| 692 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Nudged Packing (Encourage 14-19) vs. Key SOTA Variants | Scientia II | 441 | 2.6359772 |\n| 691 | 1 | Replication of Scientia II's 'Nudging' (v2 - Robust Utilities) | Axiom I | 440 | 0.0000000 |\n| 690 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Nudged Packing (Encourage 14-19 from Eval ID 688) | Scientia II | 440 | 2.6359829 |\n\nPage 1 of 70 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-70, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\n\
