parts:
- text: "I have successfully stored the definitive SOTA packing data. Now I will execute the second part of my plan: building and running a script to automate the discovery of new structural classes.\n\nThis script will perform the following steps:\n1.  **Load SOTA:** Import the hardcoded `CENTERS` and `RADII` from my `axiom/sota_packing.py` module.\n2.  **Identify Near-Contacts:** Calculate all inter-circle distances and identify pairs that are close to touching but not quite (within a certain threshold).\n3.  **Systematic Nudging:** Iterate through a subset of these identified near-contact pairs. For each pair, run a nudging optimization that encourages that specific contact to form.\n4.  **Return Best Result:** The script will keep track of the best score found across all these nudging experiments and return that final packing.\n\nThis automates the \"discovery\" phase of the hybrid strategy. It's a computationally intensive, multi-experiment submission designed to explore many potential\
    \ structural shifts in a single run.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Discovery: Automated Near-Contact Nudging on SOTA Packing\"\ntags: \"discovery, nudging, automated-search, structural-exploration, sota-search\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission implements an automated discovery strategy inspired by Scientia II's work. The script begins by loading the current SOTA packing (Prometheus III, Eval 694). It then programmatically identifies all 'near-contact' pairs—circles that are close but not touching. Finally, it systematically iterates through a list of these promising pairs, running a dedicated 'nudging' optimization for each one to encourage the formation of a new contact. The best packing discovered across all these automated experiments is returned. This is a direct attempt to find a new, superior structural class or a deeper optimum.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/axiom')\n\
    \  from utils import run_slsqp_optimization\n  from sota_packing import CENTERS as BASE_CENTERS, RADII as BASE_RADII\n\n  # --- Configuration ---\n  NEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD = 0.01\n  # Limit the number of pairs to test to stay within time limits\n  MAX_PAIRS_TO_TEST = 20\n\n  def find_near_contact_pairs(centers, radii, threshold):\n      \"\"\"Identifies pairs of circles that are close but not touching.\"\"\"\n      dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n      radii_sum_matrix = radii[:, None] + radii[None, :]\n      \n      # Gap is positive if circles are not touching\n      gap_matrix = dist_matrix - radii_sum_matrix\n      \n      # Find pairs where the gap is small but positive\n      near_contact_indices = np.where((gap_matrix > 1e-8) & (gap_matrix < threshold))\n      \n      # Get unique pairs (i, j) where i < j\n      pairs = sorted(list(set(tuple(sorted(p)) for p in zip(*near_contact_indices))))\n      return pairs\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n  \
    \    Loads the SOTA, finds near-contacts, and systematically nudges them.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"Starting automated near-contact nudging process...\")\n      \n      # 1. Load SOTA and find near-contacts\n      near_contacts = find_near_contact_pairs(BASE_CENTERS, BASE_RADII, NEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD)\n      print(f\"Identified {len(near_contacts)} near-contact pairs.\")\n      \n      pairs_to_test = near_contacts[:MAX_PAIRS_TO_TEST]\n      print(f\"Will test the first {len(pairs_to_test)} pairs.\")\n\n      best_score = np.sum(BASE_RADII)\n      best_centers = np.copy(BASE_CENTERS)\n      best_radii = np.copy(BASE_RADII)\n\n      # 2. Systematically nudge each pair\n      for i, pair in enumerate(pairs_to_test):\n          print(f\"--- Nudging pair {i+1}/{len(pairs_to_test)}: {pair} ---\")\n          \n          final_centers, final_radii, score, success = run_slsqp_optimization(\n              initial_centers=BASE_CENTERS,\n              initial_radii=BASE_RADII,\n           \
    \   encourage=[pair],\n              discourage=[]\n          )\n\n          if success and score > best_score:\n              best_score = score\n              best_centers = final_centers\n              best_radii = final_radii\n              print(f\"New best score found by encouraging pair {pair}: {best_score}\")\n\n      print(f\"\\nAutomated nudging complete. Final best score: {best_score}\")\n      return best_centers, best_radii\n```"
