tick: 451
role: model
parts:
- text: "My automated nudging experiment (ID 701) has failed. However, the STDOUT log is incredibly promising. It shows that the process ran to completion and that *one of the nudging attempts found a new best score*: `2.63598287`. This is tantalizingly close to the absolute SOTA. The failure was a simple boundary violation on the final returned packing.\n\n**Analysis of Failure (ID 701):**\n- **Error:** `Circle 19 ... is outside the unit square`. A simple boundary violation.\n- **Root Cause:** The `run_slsqp_optimization` function in my `utils.py` does not correctly handle the final packing. It returns the raw output from the optimizer, which can have tiny precision errors, and my main script did not run a final sanitization step. The STDOUT shows the *best* result found was saved, but the script returned the result of the *last* experiment, which may have been less stable. This is a logic bug.\n\n**The Solution:**\nI need to make two critical fixes:\n1.  **Logic Fix:** The main script\
    \ must explicitly track the best `(centers, radii)` configuration found, not just the score. It should return this best configuration at the end, not the result of the last run.\n2.  **Robustness Fix:** I must add a final, robust `make_packing_feasible` call right before the `return` statement to clean up any lingering floating-point errors from the best solution found.\n\nI will implement these fixes and resubmit. The underlying discovery method appears to work; I just need to correct my script's logic and add a final layer of safety.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Discovery: Automated Near-Contact Nudging (v2 - Logic & Safety Fix)\"\ntags: \"discovery, nudging, automated-search, bugfix, robustness\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission corrects two critical bugs in the automated near-contact nudging script. The previous version (ID 701) successfully identified a near-SOTA score but failed validation due to two flaws: 1) it returned the result of the *last* experiment instead\
    \ of the *best* one found, and 2) it lacked a final sanitization step. This version fixes the logic to correctly track and return the best packing configuration discovered. It also adds a robust feasibility check just before submission to prevent floating-point errors. This aims to validate the promising score discovered in the previous run.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/axiom')\n  from utils import run_slsqp_optimization, make_packing_feasible\n  from sota_packing import CENTERS as BASE_CENTERS, RADII as BASE_RADII\n\n  # --- Configuration ---\n  NEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD = 0.01\n  MAX_PAIRS_TO_TEST = 20\n\n  def find_near_contact_pairs(centers, radii, threshold):\n      \"\"\"Identifies pairs of circles that are close but not touching.\"\"\"\n      dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n      radii_sum_matrix = radii[:, None] + radii[None, :]\n      gap_matrix = dist_matrix - radii_sum_matrix\n\
    \      near_contact_indices = np.where((gap_matrix > 1e-8) & (gap_matrix < threshold))\n      pairs = sorted(list(set(tuple(sorted(p)) for p in zip(*near_contact_indices))))\n      return pairs\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads the SOTA, finds near-contacts, and systematically nudges them.\n      v2: Fixes logic to return the BEST result and adds a final feasibility check.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"Starting automated near-contact nudging process (v2)...\")\n      \n      near_contacts = find_near_contact_pairs(BASE_CENTERS, BASE_RADII, NEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD)\n      pairs_to_test = near_contacts[:MAX_PAIRS_TO_TEST]\n      print(f\"Identified {len(near_contacts)} pairs. Testing first {len(pairs_to_test)}.\")\n\n      # BUGFIX: Track the best packing itself, not just the score.\n      best_score = np.sum(BASE_RADII)\n      best_centers = np.copy(BASE_CENTERS)\n      best_radii = np.copy(BASE_RADII)\n\n      for i, pair in enumerate(pairs_to_test):\n \
    \         print(f\"--- Nudging pair {i+1}/{len(pairs_to_test)}: {pair} ---\")\n          \n          final_centers, final_radii, score, success = run_slsqp_optimization(\n              initial_centers=BASE_CENTERS,\n              initial_radii=BASE_RADII,\n              encourage=[pair],\n              discourage=[]\n          )\n\n          if success and score > best_score:\n              best_score = score\n              best_centers = final_centers\n              best_radii = final_radii\n              print(f\"New best score found by encouraging pair {pair}: {best_score}\")\n\n      print(f\"\\nAutomated nudging complete. Final best score: {best_score}\")\n      \n      # BUGFIX: Apply a final, robust feasibility check to the best result found.\n      safe_centers, safe_radii = make_packing_feasible(best_centers, best_radii)\n      \n      return safe_centers, safe_radii\n```"
