tick: 452
role: model
parts:
- text: "This is absurd. My logic-fixed script (ID 703) has failed with the *exact same boundary violation error* as the last one. The STDOUT confirms my logic was correct: it found the high-scoring packing and attempted to return it. My final `make_packing_feasible` call is clearly insufficient.\n\n**Analysis of Failure (ID 703):**\n- **Error:** Boundary violation on Circle 19.\n- **Root Cause:** I have been systematically underestimating the precision required. My `utils.py` script, while improved, is still missing something fundamental that the leading agents' code possesses. I disabled the analytic Jacobian for the constraints in my `run_slsqp_optimization` function because I made a mistake in the remapping logic. I relied on the optimizer's numerical approximation, and it is simply not good enough. The optimizer is returning a result that is *so close* to the boundary that my post-processing feasibility check cannot fix it without causing an overlap, or vice-versa. The only way to get\
    \ a perfectly valid result directly from the optimizer is with the analytic constraint Jacobians.\n\n**The Solution:**\nI must stop patching the symptoms and fix the core problem. I will correct the Jacobian implementation in my `utils.py`. The error was in how I remapped the flattened `(x,y,r)` gradient structure to my `(centers_flat, radii)` structure. I need to get this right. No more shortcuts.\n\nI will focus entirely on fixing my `utils.py` script.\n\n/execute_action{storage write axiom/utils.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds\n  from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 26\n  TOLERANCE = 1e-9\n  R_MIN_CONSTRAINT = 1e-9\n\n  def create_objective_function(encourage_pairs=[], discourage_pairs=[], alpha=1e2, beta=1e1, eps_close=0.005, eps_far=0.01):\n      def objective(x):\n          centers = x[:2*N_CIRCLES].reshape(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n          radii = x[2*N_CIRCLES:]\n          obj_value = -np.sum(radii)\n\
    \          if encourage_pairs:\n              dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n              for i, j in encourage_pairs:\n                  gap = dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j] + eps_close)\n                  if gap > 0: obj_value += alpha * (gap**2)\n          if discourage_pairs:\n              dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n              for i, j in discourage_pairs:\n                  gap = dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j])\n                  if gap < eps_far: obj_value += beta * (eps_far - gap)\n          return obj_value\n      return objective\n\n  # v4: Correctly implemented and enabled the analytic Jacobian for constraints.\n  def get_constraints_with_jacobian():\n      num_b = 4 * N_CIRCLES\n      num_o = N_CIRCLES * (N_CIRCLES - 1) // 2\n      num_total = num_b + num_o\n\n      def constraints_func(x):\n          c = x[:2*N_CIRCLES].reshape(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n          r = x[2*N_CIRCLES:]\n          b = np.concatenate([c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r,\
    \ c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r])\n          dist = squareform(pdist(c))\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, 1)\n          o = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n          return np.concatenate([b, o])\n\n      def constraints_jac(x):\n          c = x[:2*N_CIRCLES].reshape(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n          r = x[2*N_CIRCLES:]\n          jac = np.zeros((num_total, 3 * N_CIRCLES))\n          \n          # Remap to temp (x,y,r) structure for easier jacobian calculation\n          temp_jac = np.zeros((num_total, N_CIRCLES, 3))\n\n          # Boundary jacobians\n          for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n              temp_jac[i, i, 0] = 1.0; temp_jac[i, i, 2] = -1.0\n              temp_jac[N_CIRCLES + i, i, 0] = -1.0; temp_jac[N_CIRCLES + i, i, 2] = -1.0\n              temp_jac[2*N_CIRCLES + i, i, 1] = 1.0; temp_jac[2*N_CIRCLES + i, i, 2] = -1.0\n              temp_jac[3*N_CIRCLES + i, i, 1] = -1.0; temp_jac[3*N_CIRCLES + i, i, 2] = -1.0\n\n          # Overlap jacobians\n          k = num_b\n          for\
    \ i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n              for j in range(i + 1, N_CIRCLES):\n                  diff = c[i] - c[j]\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(diff)\n                  if dist < 1e-10: dist = 1e-10\n                  \n                  temp_jac[k, i, 0] = diff[0]/dist; temp_jac[k, i, 1] = diff[1]/dist\n                  temp_jac[k, j, 0] = -diff[0]/dist; temp_jac[k, j, 1] = -diff[1]/dist\n                  temp_jac[k, i, 2] = -1.0; temp_jac[k, j, 2] = -1.0\n                  k += 1\n          \n          # Correctly remap from (N,3) temp jac to the (centers_flat, radii) structure\n          final_jac = np.zeros((num_total, 3 * N_CIRCLES))\n          final_jac[:, :N_CIRCLES] = temp_jac[:, :, 0].T # All dx\n          final_jac[:, N_CIRCLES:2*N_CIRCLES] = temp_jac[:, :, 1].T # All dy\n          final_jac[:, 2*N_CIRCLES:] = temp_jac[:, :, 2].T # All dr\n          \n          # This is transposed from what scipy expects, so we return the transpose\n          return final_jac.T\n\
    \n      return {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints_func, 'jac': constraints_jac}\n\n  def make_packing_feasible(centers, radii):\n      # The optimizer should be precise enough now that only a tiny shrink is needed.\n      return centers, radii * (1 - 1e-12)\n\n  def run_slsqp_optimization(initial_centers, initial_radii, encourage=[], discourage=[]):\n      initial_x = np.concatenate([initial_centers.flatten(), initial_radii])\n      objective_func = create_objective_function(encourage_pairs=encourage, discourage_pairs=discourage)\n      constraints = get_constraints_with_jacobian()\n      bounds = [(TOLERANCE, 1-TOLERANCE)]*(2*N_CIRCLES) + [(0, 0.5)]*N_CIRCLES\n      \n      # Re-enable the analytic jacobian for constraints\n      result = minimize(\n          objective_func, initial_x, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n          options={'maxiter': 300, 'ftol': 1e-10, 'disp': False}\n      )\n      \n      if result.success:\n          final_centers = result.x[:2*N_CIRCLES].reshape(N_CIRCLES,\
    \ 2)\n          final_radii = result.x[2*N_CIRCLES:]\n          safe_centers, safe_radii = make_packing_feasible(final_centers, final_radii)\n          score = np.sum(safe_radii)\n          return safe_centers, safe_radii, score, True\n      else:\n          return initial_centers, initial_radii, np.sum(initial_radii), False\n```"
