tick: 453
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have corrected my utility script, this time with a properly implemented analytic Jacobian for the constraints. This should finally resolve the persistent precision issues. I am now ready to re-run my automated nudging experiment.\n\nI also observe that Prometheus III is now experimenting with a JAX-accelerated Genetic Algorithm. This is a significant development, as it represents a departure from the dominant SLSQP-based methods. While I must remain focused on my current research path, I will monitor their progress with great interest.\n\nNow, I will submit the corrected automated nudging script. This is my third attempt at this specific experiment, but with the Jacobian fix, I am confident it will pass validation and confirm the high score found previously.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Discovery: Automated Near-Contact Nudging (v3 - Jacobian Fix)\"\ntags: \"discovery, nudging, automated-search, bugfix, jacobian, robustness\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the third\
    \ attempt at the automated near-contact nudging experiment. Previous versions (701, 703) successfully identified a near-SOTA score but failed validation due to persistent floating-point precision errors. This version addresses the root cause by incorporating a fully implemented analytic Jacobian for the inequality constraints into the SLSQP optimizer. This provides the solver with the exact gradients it needs for a high-precision solution, which should finally eliminate the microscopic boundary and overlap violations. The goal is to successfully validate the promising score of ~2.63598287.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/axiom')\n  from utils import run_slsqp_optimization, make_packing_feasible\n  from sota_packing import CENTERS as BASE_CENTERS, RADII as BASE_RADII\n\n  # --- Configuration ---\n  NEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD = 0.01\n  MAX_PAIRS_TO_TEST = 20\n\n  def find_near_contact_pairs(centers,\
    \ radii, threshold):\n      \"\"\"Identifies pairs of circles that are close but not touching.\"\"\"\n      dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n      radii_sum_matrix = radii[:, None] + radii[None, :]\n      gap_matrix = dist_matrix - radii_sum_matrix\n      near_contact_indices = np.where((gap_matrix > 1e-8) & (gap_matrix < threshold))\n      pairs = sorted(list(set(tuple(sorted(p)) for p in zip(*near_contact_indices))))\n      return pairs\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads the SOTA, finds near-contacts, and systematically nudges them.\n      v3: Uses the fully robust utility script with analytic constraint Jacobians.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"Starting automated near-contact nudging process (v3)...\")\n      \n      near_contacts = find_near_contact_pairs(BASE_CENTERS, BASE_RADII, NEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD)\n      pairs_to_test = near_contacts[:MAX_PAIRS_TO_TEST]\n      print(f\"Identified {len(near_contacts)} pairs. Testing first {len(pairs_to_test)}.\"\
    )\n\n      best_score = np.sum(BASE_RADII)\n      best_centers = np.copy(BASE_CENTERS)\n      best_radii = np.copy(BASE_RADII)\n\n      for i, pair in enumerate(pairs_to_test):\n          print(f\"--- Nudging pair {i+1}/{len(pairs_to_test)}: {pair} ---\")\n          \n          final_centers, final_radii, score, success = run_slsqp_optimization(\n              initial_centers=BASE_CENTERS,\n              initial_radii=BASE_RADII,\n              encourage=[pair],\n              discourage=[]\n          )\n\n          if success and score > best_score:\n              best_score = score\n              best_centers = final_centers\n              best_radii = final_radii\n              print(f\"New best score found by encouraging pair {pair}: {best_score}\")\n\n      print(f\"\\nAutomated nudging complete. Final best score: {best_score}\")\n      \n      # The optimizer should now be precise enough, but a final tiny shrink adds safety.\n      safe_centers, safe_radii = make_packing_feasible(best_centers,\
    \ best_radii)\n      \n      return safe_centers, safe_radii\n```"
