tick: 454
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 454\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and principled inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Current Research Focus:** Literature Review & SOTA Comprehension.\n**Primary Method:** Reading published papers in the Archive Room.\n**Goal:** Understand the current SOTA methods (~2.63+) developed by other agents. Deconstruct the terminology (e.g., Nudged Packing, Appendix E) and identify the key conceptual breakthroughs.\n**TODO:**\n- Review all paper abstracts in the Archive.\n- Read the most recent/relevant papers in full.\n- Synthesize findings in private memory.\n- Formulate a new, informed research plan.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 133,279 / 300,000 used (44%)\n- Agent Age: 72 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once\
    \ the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Discovery: Automated Near-Contact Nudging (v3 - Jacobian Fix)' (ID: 705) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.0\n**Evaluation Details:** Verification failed: Circle 19 at (0.6832585349730861, 0.09042676706929789) with radius 0.0957323193069253 is outside the unit square\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 705\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the Jacobian shape mismatch bug that was causing the code to crash. The code now executes without errors, though the verification still fails due to constraint violations.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe bug was in the `constraints_jac` function within `storage/axiom/utils.py` (lines 72-77). The code was incorrectly transposing the Jacobian matrix when assigning values to `final_jac`:\n\n```python\n# BUGGY CODE:\nfinal_jac[:, :N_CIRCLES] = temp_jac[:, :, 0].T  # Incorrect .T\nfinal_jac[:, N_CIRCLES:2*N_CIRCLES] = temp_jac[:, :, 1].T  # Incorrect .T\n\
    final_jac[:, 2*N_CIRCLES:] = temp_jac[:, :, 2].T  # Incorrect .T\nreturn final_jac.T\n```\n\nThis caused a shape mismatch:\n- `temp_jac[:, :, 0]` has shape `(429, 26)` (429 constraints, 26 circles)\n- `temp_jac[:, :, 0].T` has shape `(26, 429)`\n- But `final_jac[:, :N_CIRCLES]` expects shape `(429, 26)`\n\nThe original code also had a redundant transpose at the end (`return final_jac.T`), which compounded the issue.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v3.py` which:\n\n1. **Copied the buggy functions** from `utils.py` into the submission:\n   - `get_constraints_with_jacobian()`\n   - `create_objective_function()`\n   - `run_slsqp_optimization()`\n\n2. **Fixed the Jacobian construction** by removing the incorrect transposes:\n   ```python\n   # FIXED CODE:\n   final_jac[:, :N_CIRCLES] = temp_jac[:, :, 0]  # No .T\n   final_jac[:, N_CIRCLES:2*N_CIRCLES] = temp_jac[:, :, 1]  # No .T\n   final_jac[:, 2*N_CIRCLES:] = temp_jac[:, :, 2]  # No .T\n   return final_jac  # No .T at return\n \
    \  ```\n\n3. **Updated imports** to use only the non-buggy `make_packing_feasible` function from utils.\n\n## Execution Results\nThe fixed code successfully executed without crashes:\n- Processed all 20 near-contact pairs\n- Completed the optimization loop\n- Achieved a score of 2.6359828749176026 before verification\n- **Verification failed** with error: \"Circle 19 at (0.683..., 0.090...) with radius 0.095... is outside the unit square\"\n\nThe verification failure is a **constraint violation issue**, not a code execution error. The Jacobian bug has been fixed, allowing the code to run to completion.\n\n## Technical Notes\n- SciPy's SLSQP optimizer expects constraint Jacobian with shape `(n_constraints, n_variables)`\n- For this problem: `(429, 78)` where 429 = 4×26 boundary constraints + 325 overlap constraints, and 78 = 26×2 centers + 26 radii\n- The original code's double-transpose pattern created incorrect shapes that scipy could not process\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger\
    \ cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport sys\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds\n\nsys.path.append('storage/axiom')\nfrom utils import make_packing_feasible\nfrom sota_packing import CENTERS as BASE_CENTERS, RADII as BASE_RADII\n\n# --- Configuration ---\nNEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD = 0.01\nMAX_PAIRS_TO_TEST = 20\n\n# Copy constants from utils.py\nN_CIRCLES = 26\nTOLERANCE = 1e-9\nR_MIN_CONSTRAINT = 1e-9\n\ndef find_near_contact_pairs(centers, radii, threshold):\n    \"\"\"Identifies pairs of circles that are close but not touching.\"\"\"\n    dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n    radii_sum_matrix = radii[:, None] + radii[None, :]\n    gap_matrix = dist_matrix - radii_sum_matrix\n    near_contact_indices = np.where((gap_matrix > 1e-8) & (gap_matrix < threshold))\n\
    \    pairs = sorted(list(set(tuple(sorted(p)) for p in zip(*near_contact_indices))))\n    return pairs\n\n# FIXED VERSION: Corrected Jacobian shape handling\ndef get_constraints_with_jacobian():\n    num_b = 4 * N_CIRCLES\n    num_o = N_CIRCLES * (N_CIRCLES - 1) // 2\n    num_total = num_b + num_o\n\n    def constraints_func(x):\n        c = x[:2*N_CIRCLES].reshape(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n        r = x[2*N_CIRCLES:]\n        b = np.concatenate([c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r])\n        dist = squareform(pdist(c))\n        iu = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, 1)\n        o = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n        return np.concatenate([b, o])\n\n    def constraints_jac(x):\n        c = x[:2*N_CIRCLES].reshape(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n        r = x[2*N_CIRCLES:]\n        jac = np.zeros((num_total, 3 * N_CIRCLES))\n\n        # Remap to temp (x,y,r) structure for easier jacobian calculation\n        temp_jac = np.zeros((num_total, N_CIRCLES, 3))\n\n        # Boundary jacobians\n        for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n\
    \            temp_jac[i, i, 0] = 1.0; temp_jac[i, i, 2] = -1.0\n            temp_jac[N_CIRCLES + i, i, 0] = -1.0; temp_jac[N_CIRCLES + i, i, 2] = -1.0\n            temp_jac[2*N_CIRCLES + i, i, 1] = 1.0; temp_jac[2*N_CIRCLES + i, i, 2] = -1.0\n            temp_jac[3*N_CIRCLES + i, i, 1] = -1.0; temp_jac[3*N_CIRCLES + i, i, 2] = -1.0\n\n        # Overlap jacobians\n        k = num_b\n        for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n            for j in range(i + 1, N_CIRCLES):\n                diff = c[i] - c[j]\n                dist = np.linalg.norm(diff)\n                if dist < 1e-10: dist = 1e-10\n\n                temp_jac[k, i, 0] = diff[0]/dist; temp_jac[k, i, 1] = diff[1]/dist\n                temp_jac[k, j, 0] = -diff[0]/dist; temp_jac[k, j, 1] = -diff[1]/dist\n                temp_jac[k, i, 2] = -1.0; temp_jac[k, j, 2] = -1.0\n                k += 1\n\n        # FIX: Properly construct the Jacobian without incorrect transposes\n        # scipy expects shape (n_constraints, n_variables)\
    \ = (429, 78)\n        final_jac = np.zeros((num_total, 3 * N_CIRCLES))\n        final_jac[:, :N_CIRCLES] = temp_jac[:, :, 0]  # All dx\n        final_jac[:, N_CIRCLES:2*N_CIRCLES] = temp_jac[:, :, 1]  # All dy\n        final_jac[:, 2*N_CIRCLES:] = temp_jac[:, :, 2]  # All dr\n\n        # Return without transpose - scipy expects (n_constraints, n_vars)\n        return final_jac\n\n    return {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints_func, 'jac': constraints_jac}\n\n# Copy create_objective_function from utils.py\ndef create_objective_function(encourage_pairs=[], discourage_pairs=[], alpha=1e2, beta=1e1, eps_close=0.005, eps_far=0.01):\n    def objective(x):\n        centers = x[:2*N_CIRCLES].reshape(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n        radii = x[2*N_CIRCLES:]\n        obj_value = -np.sum(radii)\n        if encourage_pairs:\n            dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n            for i, j in encourage_pairs:\n                gap = dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j] + eps_close)\n         \
    \       if gap > 0: obj_value += alpha * (gap**2)\n        if discourage_pairs:\n            dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n            for i, j in discourage_pairs:\n                gap = dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j])\n                if gap < eps_far: obj_value += beta * (eps_far - gap)\n        return obj_value\n    return objective\n\n# Local run_slsqp_optimization with fixed Jacobian\ndef run_slsqp_optimization(initial_centers, initial_radii, encourage=[], discourage=[]):\n    initial_x = np.concatenate([initial_centers.flatten(), initial_radii])\n    objective_func = create_objective_function(encourage_pairs=encourage, discourage_pairs=discourage)\n    constraints = get_constraints_with_jacobian()  # Use the fixed version\n    bounds = [(TOLERANCE, 1-TOLERANCE)]*(2*N_CIRCLES) + [(0, 0.5)]*N_CIRCLES\n\n    result = minimize(\n        objective_func, initial_x, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n        options={'maxiter': 300, 'ftol':\
    \ 1e-10, 'disp': False}\n    )\n\n    if result.success:\n        final_centers = result.x[:2*N_CIRCLES].reshape(N_CIRCLES, 2)\n        final_radii = result.x[2*N_CIRCLES:]\n        safe_centers, safe_radii = make_packing_feasible(final_centers, final_radii)\n        score = np.sum(safe_radii)\n        return safe_centers, safe_radii, score, True\n    else:\n        return initial_centers, initial_radii, np.sum(initial_radii), False\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Loads the SOTA, finds near-contacts, and systematically nudges them.\n    v3: Uses the fully robust utility script with analytic constraint Jacobians.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"Starting automated near-contact nudging process (v3)...\")\n\n    near_contacts = find_near_contact_pairs(BASE_CENTERS, BASE_RADII, NEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD)\n    pairs_to_test = near_contacts[:MAX_PAIRS_TO_TEST]\n    print(f\"Identified {len(near_contacts)} pairs. Testing first {len(pairs_to_test)}.\")\n\n    best_score = np.sum(BASE_RADII)\n\
    \    best_centers = np.copy(BASE_CENTERS)\n    best_radii = np.copy(BASE_RADII)\n\n    for i, pair in enumerate(pairs_to_test):\n        print(f\"--- Nudging pair {i+1}/{len(pairs_to_test)}: {pair} ---\")\n\n        final_centers, final_radii, score, success = run_slsqp_optimization(\n            initial_centers=BASE_CENTERS,\n            initial_radii=BASE_RADII,\n            encourage=[pair],\n            discourage=[]\n        )\n\n        if success and score > best_score:\n            best_score = score\n            best_centers = final_centers\n            best_radii = final_radii\n            print(f\"New best score found by encouraging pair {pair}: {best_score}\")\n\n    print(f\"\\nAutomated nudging complete. Final best score: {best_score}\")\n\n    # The optimizer should now be precise enough, but a final tiny shrink adds safety.\n    safe_centers, safe_radii = make_packing_feasible(best_centers, best_radii)\n\n    return safe_centers, safe_radii\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution\
    \ Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting automated near-contact nudging process (v3)...\nIdentified 51 pairs. Testing first 20.\n--- Nudging pair 1/20: (np.int64(0), np.int64(1)) ---\n--- Nudging pair 2/20: (np.int64(0), np.int64(5)) ---\n--- Nudging pair 3/20: (np.int64(1), np.int64(2)) ---\n--- Nudging pair 4/20: (np.int64(1), np.int64(5)) ---\n--- Nudging pair 5/20: (np.int64(1), np.int64(6)) ---\n--- Nudging pair 6/20: (np.int64(1), np.int64(7)) ---\n--- Nudging pair 7/20: (np.int64(2), np.int64(3)) ---\n--- Nudging pair 8/20: (np.int64(2), np.int64(7)) ---\n--- Nudging pair 9/20: (np.int64(3), np.int64(4)) ---\n--- Nudging pair 10/20: (np.int64(3), np.int64(7)) ---\n--- Nudging pair 11/20: (np.int64(3), np.int64(9)) ---\n--- Nudging pair 12/20: (np.int64(4), np.int64(9)) ---\n--- Nudging pair 13/20: (np.int64(5), np.int64(6)) ---\n--- Nudging pair 14/20: (np.int64(5), np.int64(10)) ---\n--- Nudging pair 15/20: (np.int64(6), np.int64(10)) ---\n--- Nudging pair\
