role: model
parts:
- text: "I have implemented the final, definitive fix to my utility script. The tolerance has been tightened, the sanitizer is more aggressive, and the optimizer settings are stricter. I am now ready to run the automated nudging experiment for the sixth time. I am confident that the precision issues are resolved.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Discovery: Automated Near-Contact Nudging (v6 - Precision Fix)\"\ntags: \"discovery, nudging, automated-search, bugfix, precision, robustness\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the sixth attempt at the automated near-contact nudging experiment. All five previous attempts failed validation despite finding a high-quality score internally. A deep analysis revealed the root cause to be a tolerance mismatch between my sanitization function and the evaluator. This version addresses this by dramatically tightening the tolerance parameters within the optimizer and the final feasibility function. This experiment aims to finally pass validation by producing\
    \ a solution that is correct to the highest required degree of floating-point precision, validating the near-SOTA score of ~2.63598287.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n\n  # Use the final, fully corrected v6 of the utility script\n  sys.path.append('storage/axiom')\n  from utils import run_slsqp_optimization\n  from sota_packing import CENTERS as BASE_CENTERS, RADII as BASE_RADII\n\n  # --- Configuration ---\n  NEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD = 0.01\n  MAX_PAIRS_TO_TEST = 20\n\n  def find_near_contact_pairs(centers, radii, threshold):\n      dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n      radii_sum_matrix = radii[:, None] + radii[None, :]\n      gap_matrix = dist_matrix - radii_sum_matrix\n      near_contact_indices = np.where((gap_matrix > 1e-8) & (gap_matrix < threshold))\n      pairs = sorted(list(set(tuple(sorted(p)) for p in zip(*near_contact_indices))))\n      return pairs\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n \
    \     \"\"\"\n      v6: Uses the final toolkit with the corrected precision/tolerance settings.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"Starting automated near-contact nudging process (v6)...\")\n      \n      near_contacts = find_near_contact_pairs(BASE_CENTERS, BASE_RADII, NEAR_CONTACT_THRESHOLD)\n      pairs_to_test = near_contacts[:MAX_PAIRS_TO_TEST]\n      print(f\"Identified {len(near_contacts)} pairs. Testing first {len(pairs_to_test)}.\")\n\n      best_score = np.sum(BASE_RADII)\n      best_centers = np.copy(BASE_CENTERS)\n      best_radii = np.copy(BASE_RADII)\n\n      for i, pair in enumerate(pairs_to_test):\n          print(f\"--- Nudging pair {i+1}/{len(pairs_to_test)}: {pair} ---\")\n          \n          final_centers, final_radii, score, success = run_slsqp_optimization(\n              initial_centers=BASE_CENTERS,\n              initial_radii=BASE_RADII,\n              encourage=[pair],\n              discourage=[]\n          )\n\n          if success and score > best_score:\n \
    \             best_score = score\n              best_centers = final_centers\n              best_radii = final_radii\n              print(f\"New best score found by encouraging pair {pair}: {best_score}\")\n\n      print(f\"\\nAutomated nudging complete. Final best score: {best_score}\")\n      \n      return best_centers, best_radii\n```"
